* {{rhymes|yrl|i}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|yrl|pronouns}}

# {{lb|yrl|second-class}} third-person singular personal pronoun ([[he]], [[him]], [[his]], [[she]], [[her]], [[it]], [[its]])
#: {{ux|yrl|'''I''' akanhemu uikú nhaãsé '''i''' kirá uikú.|translation='''He''' is scared because '''he''' is fat.}}
#: {{ux|yrl|Indé reputari repitá '''i''' irũmu.|translation=You want to stay with '''him'''.}}
#: {{ux|yrl|Indé remeẽ manungara '''i''' xupé.|translation=You give something to '''him'''.}}
#: {{ux|yrl|'''I''' manha uwiké uka pisasú upé.|translation='''His''' mother enters the new house.}}

====Usage notes====
* As a second-class pronoun, {{m|yrl||i}} is used as the subject of a sentence when its verb is a second-class one (those verbs are sometimes referred to as adjectives). The personal pronoun {{m|yrl||i}} is also used when governed by any postposition with the exception of {{l|yrl|arama}}. Unlike other second-class pronouns, {{m|yrl||i}} is used when governed by the postposition {{l|yrl|supé}}. Finally, {{m|yrl||i}} is used as a possessive pronoun as well.

